# Dress Down's "At the beginning of the end step, sacrifice this enchantment" triggers only as an end step begins (CR 603.2,
# 513.1). Cast with flash during Bot2's end step on turn 2, once that step has begun, it missed that beginning: it is still
# on the battlefield through Bot1's turn 3 - its Ornithopter without flying in turn 3's main phase - and is sacrificed only
# when turn 3's end step begins. On turn 4 the Ornithopter has flying again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Dress Down
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dress Down.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Mox Sapphire; Ornithopter; Dress Down
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = (absent)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Graveyard = Dress Down
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
